{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1160920-asking-help-in-translating-dreaming-concepts-to-lost","id":1160920,"title":"Asking help in translating Dreaming concepts to Lost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T11:21:42-08:00","id":1160920,"title":"Asking help in translating Dreaming concepts to Lost","content":"So, I finally bit the bullet and got the pdf of C20, and I must say: WHERE WERE YOU IN THE ORIGINAL CWOD!? WHERE!?<br /> <br /> To put it simply, I like it, whereas before, the first Dreaming book I read (and threw against the wall) was The Autumn People. However, I am primarily a Lost fan, so I'm more likely to translate things from Dreaming to Lost.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm here, asking for more experienced help when fishing for suggestions.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head: <br /> <br /> * Lost changelings and Kithain both exist and are often grudging allies. The Lost have an understandable suspicion of everything originally Arcadian, while Kithain are weirded out by how Lost are Banality-tolerant (and in fact Banality is largely responsible for Lost freedom, as it helped restore their minds after being tormented by Fomorians), but both recognize the other has a right to live, and they both hate Thallain.<br /> <br /> * Huntsmen are adhene who were brainwashed by the Fomorians by having their heart removed and one of their Legacies replaced. This caused them to lose a lot of their distinction from each other, as they're all partially hybrids between themselves and the same type of primal fae.They know what they are, and they hate it-restoring their heart is likely to earn a friend for life, though you have to find it first.<br /> <br /> * Bridge-burners sponsor the Bellrophon Institute and are secretly who conviced Anton Stark Dreamers were suffering the same mental disorder as part of their quest to ruin Earth so badly the Fomorians lose interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:19:31-08:00","id":1168552,"title":"","content":"Some Ideas<br /> <br /> The Hedge is the border to the Silver gate and The Lost could be the kithain's key to returning to Arcadia because they aren't locked out.<br /> <br /> Dauntain are what happens when a Keeper takes an unawakened Kithain. They are Kithain's fetches. OR Fetches are kithain.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblin=Chimera obviously.<br /> <br /> Goblin fruit could be a special type of natural dross that Kithain can harvest <br /> <br /> If you are having Lost track Banality, strengthening the mask could be a trigger.<br /> <br /> In many ways the Lost and the Kithain are inversions of eachother. The Lost are humans that have to struggle wth becoming more fae, while the Kithain are far that have to struggle with becoming more human. That makes for an interesting story seed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T22:46:22-08:00","id":1168722,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can't imagine the Lost having anything but vehement animosity towards the Kithian, on account of the latter literally being Fae wrapped in human flesh.<br /> <br /> Actually, let me dial it back. It would probably depend on the individual Kith and Court, with some hating the Kithian more than others. On the whole, though, I imagine the one group would distrust and distance themselves from the other, as a rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T00:24:13-08:00","id":1168731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimalcoatl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1160920-asking-help-in-translating-dreaming-concepts-to-lost?p=1168552#post1168552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many ways the Lost and the Kithain are inversions of eachother. The Lost are humans that have to struggle wth becoming more fae, while the Kithain are far that have to struggle with becoming more human. That makes for an interesting story seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The two gamelines are polar opposites of each other in some vary interesting ways:<ul><li><i>Changeling the Lost</i> is a game about having something terrible and horrible happening to you and you are trying to recover from and move on from those horrible events that scarred you.</li> <li><i>Changeling the Dreaming</i> is a game about having something wonderful and amazing happen to you...and you have to watch as that wonderful thing gets taken from you, not just Banality, but from time itself.</li> </ul><br /> ...actually now that I think about it, I'm kind of disappointed a Changeling translation guide wasn't one of the stretch goals. Huh. Oh well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T07:55:00-08:00","id":1168795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1160920-asking-help-in-translating-dreaming-concepts-to-lost?p=1168722#post1168722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I can't imagine the Lost having anything but vehement animosity towards the Kithian, on account of the latter literally being Fae wrapped in human flesh.<br /> <br /> Actually, let me dial it back. It would probably depend on the individual Kith and Court, with some hating the Kithian more than others. On the whole, though, I imagine the one group would distrust and distance themselves from the other, as a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lost bring hostile to the Kithain is also reliant on the Lost in question recognizing what the Kithain is. A part human, part fae being that has a mortal appearance that mortals see, a fae like appearance that fae creatures see, and calls itself a Changeling? Sounds a lot like one of the Lost at first blush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:18:27-08:00","id":1168900,"title":"","content":"It's really not tough to reconcile the two games. Just treat Lost changelings as Gallain instead of Kithain. The Gentry and their actions would be a result of the Sidhe having no commoners to entertain/serve them during the Interregnum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19264-slanzer","name":"Slanzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T00:02:27-08:00","id":1169024,"title":"","content":"Post-human beings whose souls are that of ancient beings straight from myths and legends, connected to an otherworld shaped by the collective dreams of humanity, who are mostly human-looking but can reveal their true natures at some times, and who draw upon humans\u2019 psychic energy for power? Am I talking about Kithain from Dreaming, or the Begotten from Beast?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d actually start by having the Kithain be the Bright Dream\u2019s equivalents of Beasts, and then expand their playground to the Dreaming Roads of the Hedge to connect them to the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T18:33:55-08:00","id":1169242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1160920-asking-help-in-translating-dreaming-concepts-to-lost?p=1169024#post1169024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post-human beings whose souls are that of ancient beings straight from myths and legends, connected to an otherworld shaped by the collective dreams of humanity, who are mostly human-looking but can reveal their true natures at some times, and who draw upon humans\u2019 psychic energy for power? Am I talking about Kithain from Dreaming, or the Begotten from Beast?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d actually start by having the Kithain be the Bright Dream\u2019s equivalents of Beasts, and then expand their playground to the Dreaming Roads of the Hedge to connect them to the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right down to how, the changelings believe that the other supernatural splats, calling them Prodigals, are kin and formerly creatures of the Dreaming themselves. They just all forgot that's where they came from. As well as C20 and BtP having the same line developer...<br /> <br /> Although for me, Beasts are more like the CofD equivalent of the Thallain: what with being creatures of nightmare and fear versus the kithain being creatures of dreams and wonder.<br /> <br /> Anyways, made this post in the CtL2 KS thread on the idea of the Dreaming changelings becoming the Gentry in Lost:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1158431-changeling-kickstarter-discussion?p=1168930#post1168930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...once the Long Winter/End Times hit, some of the changelings managed to figure out how to get back to Arcadia. And as such, were able to survive the wave of Banality and not get Undone. But they still require some kind of sustenance from humanity...but since they can't step into the Autumn World anymore, they have to resort to enticing and kidnapping humans. What was previously the Enchanted start to become the Lost changelings.<br /> <br /> Not that the Dreaming changelings as abusers wasn't a huge leap: reading through the various methods of gaining Glamour, there was an undercurrent of them engaging in some pretty heinous abusive behavior. Ravaging and Rhapsody obviously, but even Musing, the most encouraged form of the Epiphanies, has the air of engaging in codependent relationships. That the Dreamer can only create art with the assistance of the changeling. In combination of the diminishing returns of Glamour as the Dreamer keeps struggling to create art with the same amount of impact with the same amount of Glamour. It wouldn't take much for a changeling to decide to just abandon the Dreamer and move on to a different one, without really caring about the state of the Dreamer. Also, since the Dreaming can be just as toxic of a place as the Autumn World and actually drives them closer to Bedlam (which in Dreaming is a different thing then in Lost). Which could explain the Gentry's demeanor and reasoning being so inhuman, could explain why they're so incapable of empathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T18:52:14-08:00","id":1169248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1160920-asking-help-in-translating-dreaming-concepts-to-lost?p=1169242#post1169242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right down to how, the changelings believe that the other supernatural splats, calling them Prodigals, are kin and formerly creatures of the Dreaming themselves. They just all forgot that's where they came from. As well as C20 and BtP having the same line developer...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Begotten, too, claim almost all other supernaturals as their Kin, in a metaphorical sense. As dream-creatures, though, a metaphor is real enough for them.<br /> <br /> So they had the same line developer, huh? No wonder they\u2019re similar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although for me, Beasts are more like the CofD equivalent of the Thallain: what with being creatures of nightmare and fear versus the kithain being creatures of dreams and wonder. </div> </div> </div>Yup. Which is why I suggested porting Kithain to CofD as creatures of the Bright Dream. The contrast between the civilized and animalistic sides of humanity\u2019s collective unconsciousness draws a nice parallel to the wondrous dreams of the Kithain and nightmarish dreams of the Thallain. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, made this post in the CtL2 KS thread on the idea of the Dreaming changelings becoming the Gentry in Lost:<br /> </div> </div> </div>Saw that as well. A Bad End of sorts for the Kithain, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T00:02:24-08:00","id":1169285,"title":"","content":"Put this on the CtL thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that makes it easier to go from CtD Changelings to Gentry is the fact that, as explained on page 301 the Sidhe frailty is replaced with Emphatic Blindness when they enter the Dreaming making them unable to think non-Nobles as beings of conseguence and in the Deep Dreaming they can barely tolerate Commoner presented at all preferring to act through proxy since it is a privilidge to hear their beautiful voices and be in their presence. So if they think so little of their fellow Changelings just think how little humans matter to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T10:12:46-08:00","id":1169671,"title":"","content":"I think you have to go more one way then the other. Like say keep The Lost setting but put a lot of Dreaming elements into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}